1
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:14,315
A long time ago, people were very different from the way we are now.

2
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:23,840
For example, if you find a really old house somewhere, you’ll see that the doors are usually much lower than they are today.

3
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:25,140
Why?

4
00:00:25,940 --> 00:00:29,360
Because hundreds of years ago, people were shorter.

5
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:35,852
Over time, the human body changes to adapt to a new way of life.

6
00:00:36,740 --> 00:00:40,280
Can we expect the human body to change in the future?

7
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:41,480
For sure.

8
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:48,620
And the main reason is that we have more and more technology, and it is changing how we live.

9
00:00:49,540 --> 00:00:52,080
What kind of changes can we expect?

10
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:57,760
Well, no one can be 100 percent sure, but here are some possibilities.

11
00:01:01,140 --> 00:01:03,020
Let’s start with the example above.

12
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:09,242
Humans are now ten centimetres taller than 150 years ago.

13
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:14,140
So, in the future, people will probably be even taller.

14
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:21,200
Most of us now have much better food than people in the past – and so we grow more.

15
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:26,901
We’ll get weaker in more than one way.

16
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:35,062
The most important way is that our muscles will not be as strong as now because we won’t do a lot of physical work.

17
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:45,825
We are already using our feet less, and our hands more (think about computers and tablets and so on).

18
00:01:45,825 --> 00:01:55,400
So we can expect that our legs will get shorter and our feet smaller, and at the same time, our fingers will get longer.

19
00:01:56,260 --> 00:02:03,080
And our fingers and our eyes will both get better because they’ll have to do more work together.

20
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,820
Now, what about the mouth?

21
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:23,460
It’ll get smaller, perhaps, because technological improvements will mean that we don’t need to talk so much – and also because our teeth will get smaller (so mouths don’t need to be so big to keep them in).

22
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:32,960
Here’s a good one – it’s very possible that people will have four toes, not five.

23
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:43,460
The little toe really isn’t needed anymore (people who lose them don’t miss them), so it will probably disappear sometime in the future.

24
00:02:46,840 --> 00:02:55,560
And last but not least – people won’t have as much hair on their bodies as now, as we don’t need it to keep ourselves warm anymore.

25
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:58,260
Will all these things happen?

26
00:02:58,800 --> 00:03:00,100
And if so, when?

27
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:04,340
These are questions that no one can answer for sure.
